<title>UK: Morgan Stanley sets warrants on SBC.</title>
<headline>Morgan Stanley sets warrants on SBC.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank Morgan Stanley said it has issued 75,000 European-style capped call warrants, on Swiss Bank Corp registered shares.</p>
<p>One warrant controls one share.</p>
<p> STRIKE PRICE 1  0.01 CHF		 STRIKE 2 (CAP)400 CHF</p>
<p> ISSUE PRICE     354.55 CHF (INDIC)</p>
<p> EXPIRATION	10.JUL.98		PAYDATE	16.JUL.97</p>
<p> DISCOUNT TO REFERENCE PRICE 12.46 PCT (INDICATIVE)</p>
<p> MAXIMUM RETURN 12.86 PCT (P/A) INDICATIVE</p>
<p> SPOT REFERENCE  405 CHF</p>
<p> NOTES    IF SHARE PRICE AT EXPIRATION IS AT OR ABOVE</p>
<p>	    CAP LEVEL THEN RECEIVE 400 CHF. IF SHARE PRICE</p>
<p>	    IS BELOW CAP THEN RECEIVE ONE SBC REGISTERED SHARE.</p>
<p>* * * * *</p>
<p>MORGAN STANLEY TERM THE WARRANTS 'EROS' -ENHANCED RETURN OR SECURITY.</p>
<p>--Reuter London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
